## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design scalable, secure, cost-aware multi-tenant inference pipelines with strict data residency. Tests model management (canary deployments, drift detection), data governance (Purview/RBAC), and cross-region DR. Realistic latency targets and tenant isolation are central.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation (per-tenant namespaces and feature stores)
- Real-time latency targets (<100ms p99)
- Model lifecycle: registry, canary deployments, drift monitoring
- Data governance: Purview RBAC lineage, BYOK encryption in rest/transit
- Cost optimization: autoscaling, per-tenant quotas, reserved capacity

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing for tenant-aware inference (high level)
function routeRequest(req) {
  const tenant = extractTenant(req);
  const endpoint = getTenantEndpoint(tenant);
  return callModelEndpoint(endpoint, req.payload);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test canary deployments at scale?
- How would you handle tenant onboarding/offboarding and data deletion?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests real-world trade-offs for privacy, governance, and cost in Azure-native AI at scale, including per-tenant isolation, data lineage, and DR.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation with per-tenant data partitions
- Azure ML model fine-tuning strategies for tenants
- Data governance using Purview and RBAC
- BYOK with Key Vault for encryption at rest
- DR in paired regions and cost-optimized autoscale

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: resolve per-tenant resources (data path and key)
function tenantResource(tenantId){
  const dataPath = `abfss://data@storage.dfs.core.windows.net/tenants/${tenantId}/chatlogs/`;
  const keyId = `/keys/tenants/${tenantId}/chat-keys`;
  return { dataPath, keyId };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate tenant data isolation under peak load?
- What monitoring would you implement to detect model drift and data leakage?
